is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r13
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRR EIGRP process/AS on r13. Mechanism: EIGRP only forms adjacencies between routers in the same autonomous system (AS). When the AS numbers don’t match, neighbors do not come up and previously learned routes time out and are withdrawn. Localization: The broken adjacency is on the FF segment between r11.eth2 (103.1.1.1/8) and r13.eth0 (103.1.1.2/8). On r11, “show ip eigrp neighbors” shows a single neighbor 112.1.1.2 on eth0 (r12) and zero peers on eth2, while “show ip eigrp interfaces” confirms no peers on eth2. On r13, “show run” and “show ip eigrp neighbors” show EIGRP running in AS 300 with no neighbors. By contrast, r11’s EIGRP is configured for AS 100 (networks 112.0.0.0/8 and 103.0.0.0/8). Root
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=11
