[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r13
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRR EIGRP process/AS on r13. Mechanism: EIGRP only forms adjacencies between routers in the same autonomous system (AS). When the AS numbers don’t match, neighbors do not come up and previously learned routes time out and are withdrawn. Localization: The broken adjacency is on the FF segment between r11.eth2 (103.1.1.1/8) and r13.eth0 (103.1.1.2/8). On r11, “show ip eigrp neighbors” shows a single neighbor 112.1.1.2 on eth0 (r12) and zero peers on eth2, while “show ip eigrp interfaces” confirms no peers on eth2. On r13, “show run” and “show ip eigrp neighbors” show EIGRP running in AS 300 with no neighbors. By contrast, r11’s EIGRP is configured for AS 100 (networks 112.0.0.0/8 and 103.0.0.0/8). Root cause: The rollback on r13 changed its EIGRP autonomous system from 100 to 300, creating an AS mismatch with r11 and causing loss of the 113.1.x.x routes previously learned from r13. Corrective fix: Revert r13 to EIGRP AS 100 (no router eigrp 300; router eigrp 100; network 103.0.0.0/8 and 113.1.0.0/16 or the specific /24s). After aligning the AS, the EIGRP neighbor on r11.eth2 should re-establish with r13.eth0 and the 113.1.x.x routes will repopulate r11’s EIGRP topology and routing tables.
=== END ===